1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:07,360
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

2
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:13,400
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

3
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:14,660
Woah

4
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:22,760
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

5
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:25,460
nezumiiro no sora no shita

6
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:31,700
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

7
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:37,800
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

8
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:43,980
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

9
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:50,000
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

10
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:56,960
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

11
00:00:57,060 --> 00:01:02,540
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

12
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:09,140
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

13
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:14,900
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

14
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:21,100
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

15
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:28,100
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

16
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,420
[DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES]

17
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:40,220
Oh no, not again.

18
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:44,240
We've told you, you're an
important candidate for sacrifice.

19
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,000
We need you to keep your strength up.
Understand?

20
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:51,000
So, dig in, Dr. Marcoh.

21
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:54,600
You know what?
I've been sitting here a while.

22
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Trying to decide what
you mean by sacrifice.

23
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:03,400
Trying to figure out why I'm here,
and what it is exactly you want me to do.

24
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:09,430
I'm fairly certain that what
you're doing right now is using

25
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:13,280
this land and its people to
form a giant transmutation circle.

26
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,800
And your hope is that
the end result will be the

27
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,860
creation of a Philosopher's Stone.

28
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:19,000
Am I wrong?

29
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:23,000
So close. Not quite.
But you're on the right track.

30
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,000
Then what is it?

31
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:28,740
The question is, are you going
to cooperate with us or not?

32
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,140
If not, the village is history.

33
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:32,000
[GASP]

34
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:34,920
Lust told me about your arrangement.

35
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:40,220
If we agree to leave the village
alone, then you'll do whatever we ask.

36
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,000
[WHIMPERING]

37
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,380
Which is it? Agree to work with
us and kill everyone in this country?

38
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:51,000
Or refuse to work with us and watch
everyone in your beloved village die?

39
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:58,300
Fool. You just have to forsake one
little village to save an entire country.

40
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:02,300
Too bad you don't have the
stomach to do the logical thing.

41
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:06,780
I shouldn't be surprised.
That's just how all you humans are.

42
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,240
You put emotions before common sense.

43
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,640
I killed a man who was like that once.

44
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:15,120
All I had to do was make myself
look like his wife and he was helpless,

45
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,360
He couldn't even fight me.

46
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:22,020
Humans are so easy to take advantage of.
Lucky us.

47
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:37,340
The humans seem to be giving you quite
a bit of trouble lately, don't they, Wrath?

48
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:39,340
Hmm?

49
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:44,680
First Scar gets away from you,
then those others make off with Gluttony.

50
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,580
It's not like you.

51
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:49,320
Yes, you are right about that.

52
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:52,760
And yet you seem happy.

53
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,380
Yes, I won't deny it.
This has been... enjoyable.

54
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:04,640
I've been alive for 60 years and now here
I am in the ultimate position of power.

55
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:07,820
All has gone exactly as
father had planned it would.

56
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:10,000
There's more, though.

57
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:15,460
Roy Mustang and his underlings,
the enterprising Elric brothers,

58
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:18,460
and these foreigners
who suddenly appeared from Xing.

59
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:23,360
As good as we are,
they've still got us scrambling in circles.

60
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,680
Things are changing.
The time may be approaching

61
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:30,000
when we have to move over
for the younger generation.

62
00:04:30,540 --> 00:04:31,880
Don't you see?

63
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:37,820
Listen to yourself, Wrath. You've been
around these humans for far too long.

64
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:39,320
You may be right, Pride.

65
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:44,480
I hope you will stop this foolishness and
remember who we are and what we must do.

66
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,980
I won't tell father
what you've said tonight.

67
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:50,940
He might be inclined
to see it as treason.

68
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,380
Anyway, about Gluttony...

69
00:04:53,380 --> 00:04:54,940
Don't worry about that.

70
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:59,960
I have access to military information, after all.
I know where he is.

71
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:06,220
What was that?

72
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,740
Colonel! What's going on?

73
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:09,660
Hawkeye, stop!

74
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:26,680
Colonel!

75
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,720
Lieutenant!

76
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:33,560
Don't provoke him! I'm the one he wants!

77
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:35,360
Mustang!

78
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,440
Come on. We're getting out of here.

79
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:42,000
What is it? What's happening?

80
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:46,260
The Homunculus. He had another
monster hidden inside his belly.

81
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:48,560
He's swallowing up everything in sight!

82
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:53,160
Alchemy can produce something like that...

83
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:55,180
How disgusting!

84
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:57,480
Let's go. We have to bring him down.

85
00:05:57,520 --> 00:06:00,760
But we worked so hard to
catch one of the Homunculi!

86
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:05,700
Survival is our first priority.
Besides, he knows our names and faces now.

87
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,480
It would be foolish to
let him leave here alive.

88
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,960
[BURPS]

89
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:24,940
He swallowed it?

90
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:26,100
Uh-oh.

91
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:30,340
Hey, that worked well!

92
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:32,600
Think you can do better? Be my guest!

93
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:36,880
Or we can just leave you behind, Colonel!
You're the one he really wants!

94
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:40,020
Those trees over there! Spread out!

95
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,840
Damn it! Not now!

96
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:01,200
Hurry up and get in the car!

97
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:12,180
Come on! We haven't got all night!
We need to get moving!

98
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:16,450
No way! I'm a civilian, not military!

99
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:20,120
I'm not about to die in the middle of
a battle with some crazed monster!

100
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,520
Damn it!

101
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:29,400
What's taking those idiots so long?

102
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:38,740
Mustang!
[ROARS]

103
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:47,340
No!

104
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:50,000
Perfect. He fell for the Mustang decoy.

105
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:52,600
Doesn't sound like
he's very happy about it.

106
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:56,100
All right. Now get in the car, invalid.

107
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,680
Lieutenant, please take care of Lan Fan.

108
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:03,540
You expect me to run away
and leave this to you, Elric?

109
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:05,680
If you stay, you'll just get in our way!

110
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:06,780
Yeah, leave!

111
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,480
They're right.
You won't be any use here. Sorry.

112
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:13,100
How did this idiot make Colonel?

113
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:15,520
Right now you need to go and do your job.

114
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:18,120
The head of the military
is a Homunculus.

115
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:20,640
Don't you think you should
do something about that?

116
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:22,960
The head of the military?

117
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:25,840
You aren't talking about
Fuhrer Bradley, are you?

118
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:28,920
We can talk about it later. Now get in!

119
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:32,820
The car looks full. You go ahead.

120
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:34,640
You dumbasses!

121
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:38,120
You can't really believe we'll let a couple
of children fight this battle for us!

122
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:41,600
With the senior staff involved in this,
you're gonna need all the help you can get.

123
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,780
And that would include
getting whatever information

124
00:08:43,780 --> 00:08:46,420
we can out of this Gluttony
guy, wouldn't you say?

125
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:49,000
We'll stay here and find out what we can.

126
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:52,000
I don't think it matters
much that we're children.

127
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:55,920
This was our mission to begin with,
and we're going to see it through.

128
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:58,000
We appreciate your
help up till now, though.

129
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:01,240
- Here, Edward.
- Hmm?

130
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,960
I want you to take this.

131
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
You do know how to use it, don't you?

132
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:10,000
That's a weapon. For killing people.

133
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:14,000
Yes, but it's also a weapon
for protecting your lives.

134
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:22,640
It's your hands...
They weren't meant to kill.

135
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:26,680
No dying, okay?

136
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,040
I'll take it.

137
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:32,520
[CRASH]
[GASPS]

138
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,640
Look after Lan Fan.

139
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:40,720
Wait! My lord!

140
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,260
Let's go.

141
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:50,120
I said go!

142
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:54,240
Damn! What are they thinking?
Those three are gonna get themselves killed!

143
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Mustang...

144
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:09,660
Where are you, Mustang?

145
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:14,780
You killed Lust! You will pay!

146
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,000
Well, said we'd stay and all,

147
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,480
but that's seriously freaky!

148
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,760
He seems to be a bit angry.

149
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:21,860
How are we gonna catch him?

150
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,540
What was that?

151
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,160
A dog?

152
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:32,340
Stop it! Now, gluttony!

153
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:35,400
A talking dog?

154
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:38,000
Hey, long time no see.

155
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,700
How are ya, Fullmetal Pipsqueak?

156
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:51,000
Fullmetal Alchemist.

157
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:54,560
Fullmetal Alchemist.

158
00:10:55,100 --> 00:10:59,780
Damn it! I told you before!
Don't call me short!

159
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,920
Hey, calm down! I'm just here to get
Gluttony back. Nothing more than that.

160
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:07,940
- I don't wanna fight you, Pipsqueak!
- That's five, now!

161
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:09,320
What are you talking about?

162
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:12,800
Five times!
You called me Pipsqueak twice here!

163
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:15,200
And three times in the laboratory!

164
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:17,600
Don't tell me you've forgotten already!

165
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:19,980
Impressive.
You've got a sharp memory there.

166
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:21,520
Hold it!

167
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,960
You're becoming bothersome.

168
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:27,200
Mustang was here! Must avenge Lust!

169
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:28,920
Swallow! Swallow!

170
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,200
Swallow him up!

171
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:33,640
You don't get the Colonel.
Or the Elric brothers.

172
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:35,440
Why not?

173
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:38,020
I've sensed this multiplicity before.

174
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:41,260
How many people are inside you, Homunculus?

175
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:47,340
I know you. You're the kid who
crossed swords with Wrath, aren't you?

176
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:52,000
What do you mean, kid? I happen to
be the twelfth son of the Emperor of Xing!

177
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:53,880
- My name is—
- Eat him!

178
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:57,320
No! No! No! No! No! No! No! No!

179
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:00,960
You thinking what I'm thinking?

180
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Looks like they really aren't allowed
to do anything to the two of us.

181
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
[CHUCKLES] In which case...

182
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:10,240
Ling! You get that one!

183
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:15,440
Very well. Let's see how good you are.

184
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:18,800
You held off Wrath, but
how will you do against me?

185
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:21,440
Oh? Did he now?

186
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:24,280
Yes. It was the best paper in the class.

187
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:27,380
He chose to write an
essay all about you, actually.

188
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:29,760
Mom, can I read it to you guys now?

189
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:32,000
Not at the table. Mind your manners, dear.

190
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:34,120
Oh, don't be silly. Why not?

191
00:12:34,340 --> 00:12:36,540
Go ahead and read, son.
I'd like to hear it.

192
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:37,680
Great!

193
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,000
Essay on my dad.

194
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,400
He's the Führer of the nation of Amestris.

195
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:47,000
He works hard all the time, and
everything he does is for our country.

196
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:50,260
The people of Amestris
are always in his heart.

197
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:52,840
He dedicates his life to making them happy.

198
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
He deals with all sorts
of problems each day,

199
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
so everyone in our
country can live a good life.

200
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:04,500
But no matter how busy he gets doing
his job, my dad never forgets his family.

201
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:07,000
He loves me and my mother very much.

202
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
He always looks out for us.

203
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:11,000
My dad's a good man.

204
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,720
He always listens to me when I talk to him.

205
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:17,440
He's always kind and protects our family.

206
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,000
And that is why...
I love my dad. The end.

207
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,840
Thank you for that, Selim. Very much.

208
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,000
You really know how to use that thing.

209
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:30,000
Thank you for the compliment.

210
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Really!

211
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,000
You fell for it.

212
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,640
Good, isn't it?

213
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:38,140
And you humans can't do anything like it.

214
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,620
So what'll it be?

215
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:42,060
Strangled to death?
Beaten to death?

216
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:45,160
Or just carved up into little pieces?

217
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:47,000
[LAUGHS] None of the above.

218
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,220
That was a dirty trick.

219
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:07,420
Blinding me, that's not playing fair.

220
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:10,480
People have been trying to
assassinate me since I was a kid.

221
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:14,700
Under the circumstances, you can't blame
a guy for learning how to fight dirty.

222
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,460
So, have you had enough yet?

223
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:18,640
Are you going to come with me quietly now?

224
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:22,460
I just want whatever information you
can give me on becoming immortal.

225
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,320
Or shall we go again?

226
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:26,080
You scum!

227
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:28,820
A mere human like you
can't condescend to me!

228
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:30,680
You seem to underestimate humans.

229
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:32,380
And that's a mistake!

230
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:35,760
Nice! Got him!

231
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:40,640
That was a close one.

232
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:41,980
I've had enough of you!

233
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:44,000
Get away! I can't eat you!

234
00:14:44,620 --> 00:14:47,000
Just let me take a bite
from the other guy!

235
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,680
Not today!

236
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Stay out of my way, guys. I'm busy.

237
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:01,060
[GASP]

238
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:03,340
Another foolish human.

239
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:05,000
Go for it, Gluttony!

240
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Ling!

241
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:07,600
What?

242
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:11,440
Damn it! I can't let him eat a sacrifice!

243
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Brother!

244
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,240
[GASP]

245
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:40,280
Swallowed them?

246
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,200
Brother!

247
00:15:42,220 --> 00:15:43,100
Wing!

248
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:45,020
You! Spit them out!

249
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:46,360
Spit them out now!

250
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:47,160
I can't.

251
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,620
I swallowed them.

252
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:50,620
[GASP]

253
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:53,620
Impossible.

254
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,300
It can't be.

255
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,420
Brother...

256
00:15:57,380 --> 00:16:00,300
[SCREAMS]

257
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:07,000
I do have another room
that my kid used to sleep in.

258
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:10,700
But people will get suspicious
if I keep all the lights on.

259
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,660
You'll have to make do with my bed.

260
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:14,900
My lord, I have to go to him.

261
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,360
Idiot girl!

262
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,460
What can you do in your condition?

263
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
He isn't home yet?

264
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
I see.

265
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
I'll head straight to the
command center then.

266
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:42,280
Right.

267
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:43,840
Goodbye.

268
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,580
- Let's go.
-Right.

269
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,000
Go where?

270
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:53,180
I think now would be a good time to find
out who we can trust and who we can't.

271
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,420
What is it with you idiots?
You got a death wish?

272
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:59,140
Your wounds haven't
begun to heal yet and you're already

273
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:01,180
going out, looking for more trouble?

274
00:17:02,420 --> 00:17:05,380
For all we know, the
Fuhrer is a Homunculus.

275
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:07,660
I can't very well ignore that.

276
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:13,260
Besides, we just left children out
on a battlefield to do our fighting.

277
00:17:13,540 --> 00:17:17,640
If they're brave enough to fight,
how can I just sit here and wait?

278
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:22,000
What's so funny?

279
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:25,180
Oh, it's nothing really,
I was just thinking.

280
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:28,860
Can you imagine the look on Edward's
face if he heard you talking back there?

281
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,420
I was only repeating what you already said.

282
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:34,400
I have to admit, this is unexpected.

283
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:38,060
Given the situation, this is fairly
bold action for you to take, Colonel.

284
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:39,100
Like hell it is.

285
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:41,720
I'm just getting the ball
rolling, nothing more.

286
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,000
Besides...

287
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,460
You need as many people on your side
as you can get your hands on now, Colonel.

288
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:55,000
It's taken long enough, but I think I
might finally begin heeding his advice.

289
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:11,000
These are either the gates to
glory or the entranceway to hell.

290
00:18:11,540 --> 00:18:12,840
Wait here, Lieutenant.

291
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,820
If anything happens to me, then at least
you'll have a chance of getting out alive.

292
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:18,080
No, sir.

293
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:19,460
That was an order.

294
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:21,000
One that I cannot obey.

295
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:23,660
You're a stubborn one.

296
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,480
That's something you've always known, sir.

297
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:27,180
[SIGHS]

298
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
All right.

299
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Will you stay here if I
promise to come back?

300
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,000
Yes.

301
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,340
Happy hunting, sir.

302
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,220
So you're Colonel Roy Mustang, are you?

303
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:40,000
I got a call from my wife
about you a while ago.

304
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:43,000
Lieutenant General Raven, I'm sorry.

305
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,080
I haven't had time to introduce myself.

306
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:47,780
I've been very busy since my transfer.

307
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,480
It's not a problem.

308
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:53,580
Tell me, how is that old fox
Grumman doing these days anyway?

309
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,980
[CHUCKLES] The same as always, sir.

310
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:57,260
Check!

311
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:00,800
That's eleven losses in a row for me.

312
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:02,880
Twelve, actually.

313
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:06,460
But at least you put up a
decent fight this time around.

314
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:10,140
You were fine until you were
sure you'd won, then you blew it.

315
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,220
So I finished too weak?

316
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:13,100
Yes.

317
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:14,860
You can't be ruthless enough.

318
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:16,680
You're a lot like Raven that way.

319
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,720
Lieutenant General Raven?

320
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,760
From Central?

321
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,680
He's an exceptional
soldier, but too sentimental.

322
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:26,000
From what I've heard, he'll even
tend to his wounded men himself,

323
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,080
which leaves his whole
line of command in disarray.

324
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:32,100
You don't deploy your king
to tend to the pawns, do you?

325
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:34,220
How dare he say
something like that about me!

326
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:36,200
I was transferred to
Central because of the

327
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,920
compassion I showed
my men in the line of duty!

328
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:41,960
That border-dwelling old
coot should keep his trap shut!

329
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:45,180
Sorry.

330
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:46,480
No, General, it's fine.

331
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:50,000
Actually, General Grumman told
me that if that story made you angry,

332
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:54,330
it meant you were still a good and just
man, and that you were the officer one could

333
00:19:54,350 --> 00:19:57,000
come to for support in
case of an emergency.

334
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:00,620
I can't believe it.

335
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:03,200
That old fox got me again, didn't he?

336
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,840
[CHUCKLES]

337
00:20:05,340 --> 00:20:08,320
[BOTH LAUGHING]

338
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:11,260
It's time for my meeting.
Come on, you can walk with me.

339
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:16,380
Have you adjusted to Central yet?

340
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,080
No.

341
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:20,920
I find conversing with the citizens
around here quite difficult, actually.

342
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:24,500
It's a mistake to dismiss the value
of the word on the street, Colonel.

343
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:25,440
I know.

344
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:27,740
But most of it's just mindless drivel.

345
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:34,000
Like, "Scar was seen feeding a stray cat" or, "immortality has been discovered".

346
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Or maybe even that Fuhrer
Bradley is a Homunculus.

347
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Who knows?

348
00:20:40,020 --> 00:20:43,000
[BOTH LAUGHING]

349
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,320
I see, you've got no
sense of humor, do you?

350
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:47,680
Are you certain you were
one of Grumman's men?

351
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,820
His sense of humor didn't
rub off on me much, sir.

352
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:55,000
Well, at least that bit of gossip will
give us something to talk about over tea.

353
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:56,000
Huh?

354
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:59,000
I-I couldn't possibly
attend something like...

355
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,680
Go on, tell your little joke.

356
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:17,580
You know, the one about the
Fuhrer being a Homunculus.

357
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:20,100
Please, go ahead.

358
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,280
What, Colonel Mustang?

359
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:24,660
Cat got your tongue?

360
00:21:24,780 --> 00:21:29,240
Let's suppose for a moment that I
was actually a Homunculus, as you say.

361
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:32,900
Well now, would that be so bad?

362
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:41,000
Ah, I understand now, Hughes.

363
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,160
When you said that we were in trouble,

364
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:46,000
you didn't mean the
danger was closing in on us.

365
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:49,800
No, you meant the
danger was coming from us.

366
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:57,160
Well, Fullmetal, it looks like we've
landed ourselves in the pit of hell.

367
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,140
Where am I?

368
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:08,120
Blood?

369
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:10,000
What the?!

370
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,640
What is this place?

371
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:13,000
Al?

372
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:14,420
Hey!

373
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:17,160
Is anybody out there?

374
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:27,120
Where the hell am I?

375
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:34,320
Let it all out, let it all out

376
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:38,760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

377
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:45,100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

378
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:51,120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

379
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:56,680
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

380
00:22:56,680 --> 00:23:02,200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

381
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:11,960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

382
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:17,580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

383
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:23,480
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

384
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:31,540
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

385
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:33,820
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

386
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:39,340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

387
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:45,560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

388
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:53,200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

389
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:57,740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

390
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:06,280
Do you feel driven to keep searching for someone
who is lost, because you fear to be left alone,

391
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:08,280
or because you have no choice?

392
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:13,020
Because even if you cannot see them,
you cannot believe they are gone.

393
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:17,360
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

394
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:21,500
Episode 25: Doorway of Darkness

395
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:26,180
The fight continues inside the belly of the beast.
